processing technology to facilitate receipt of a taxpayers' refund proceeds; small business lending to independent tax preparation providers that seek small advances; and fast cash advance, a loan that enables tax refund recipients. Green Dot Corporation was incorporated in 1999 and is headquartered in Provo, Utah.","ceo_bio":"Mr. William I. Jacobs J.D. | CEO & Chairman of the Board | Age 83 | Compensation: $3.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 900 people. Revenue per employee of $2.3M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 11%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $73K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $21K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Green Dot Corporation is a small-cap financial services business with a $697M market cap on $2.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 67% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 57-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $66M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 1.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 4.1% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotro